# CEL — full syntax reference example

// This file demonstrates every locked CEL syntax feature in one place.
// Names are GENERIC PLACEHOLDERS — no real clinical scenario is being
// modeled. The file is a language reference, not a working test case.
//
// For grounded clinical examples, see the CMS22/CMS69 .cel files under
// features/cql-pattern-mining/results/models/cms{22,69}-split/.

library "CEL Syntax Reference".

// `covers` is required when the file has at least one case. It points to
// the CRL library whose logic this CEL library exercises.
covers "Some Strategy Library".

// `include` is only needed for EXTERNAL package libraries. Local sibling
// .cel libraries auto-resolve via qualified refs (`"Other Lib"."Fact"`)
// without an include. Aliases parse but emit `alias-not-yet-supported`.
include "External Demo Package".


// ============================================================
// Facts — the reusable, patient-agnostic clinical data points
// ============================================================

// `defined by "Patient"` — bare FHIR type from conceptTypes.json.
// The Patient class exposes name, birth date, gender, etc.
fact "Subject A":
- name is "Subject A".
- birth date is "1980-01-01".
- defined by "Patient".

// Encounter fact — provides the case's encounter context.
fact "Outpatient Visit":
- code is "http://example.org/codesystem/placeholder|VISIT-1".
- defined by "Encounter".

fact "Admission Encounter":
- code is "http://example.org/codesystem/placeholder|INPT-1".
- defined by "Encounter".

fact "Discharge Encounter":
- code is "http://example.org/codesystem/placeholder|DSCH-1".
- defined by "Encounter".

// `defined by` qualified CRL concept reference. The class declares the
// slots; the fact hydrates whatever the logic queries (here `code` and
// `value` come from the concept's declared value types).
fact "Baseline Reading":
- code is "http://example.org/codesystem/placeholder|OBS-1".
- value is 42.
- defined by "Some Strategy Library"."Some Observation".

// Same concept, different reading — facts are templates, the date is
// assigned per-case via `at`.
fact "Follow-up Reading":
- code is "http://example.org/codesystem/placeholder|OBS-1".
- value is 36.
- defined by "Some Strategy Library"."Some Observation".

// Activity-class fact. `stage is X.` comes from the activity class's
// CPG intent/status enum.
fact "Recommended Activity":
- code is "http://example.org/codesystem/placeholder|REQ-1".
- stage is proposed.
- defined by "Some Strategy Library"."Some Activity".

// Event-class fact (something that happened).
fact "Performed Event":
- code is "http://example.org/codesystem/placeholder|EVT-1".
- defined by "Procedure".

// Documentation/attestation fact — used as a positive fact to express
// "documented reason" rather than via a `documented intent` modifier
// (which is intentionally NOT in the intent enum; see #65 Q1c).
fact "Contraindication Notation":
- code is "http://example.org/codesystem/placeholder|DOC-1".
- defined by "DetectedIssue".


// ============================================================
// Cases — each one is a single scenario through the logic tree
// ============================================================

// Case 1 — `now` as the dynamic anchor for synthetic-data freshness.
// Useful when the scenario should always emit "today" relative to whenever
// the test data is regenerated.
case "Dynamic-anchor scenario":
- description is `Demonstrates `now` as the case anchor and relative
  offsets from it. The emitted FHIR resources' dates float forward
  whenever this is re-emitted.`.
- subject is "Subject A".
- encounter is "Outpatient Visit".
- anchor is now.
- fact is "Baseline Reading" at anchor.
- fact is "Recommended Activity" at anchor.
- fact is "Follow-up Reading" at anchor + 6 months.
- result is "Some Decision" is "Recommended Activity".


// Case 2 — fixed-date anchor + absolute-date escape hatch + intent variants.
case "Fixed-anchor scenario with intent variants":
- description is `Demonstrates a fixed case anchor, relative-from-anchor
  dates, the absolute-date `on` escape hatch, and the absent + negative
  intent modifiers.`.
- subject is "Subject A".
- encounter is "Outpatient Visit".
- anchor is 2026-01-15.
- fact is "Baseline Reading" at anchor.                                              // positive (default)
- fact is "Recommended Activity" at anchor with absent intent because `not proposed at this visit`.
- fact is "Recommended Activity" at anchor + 90 days with negative intent because `subject declined the proposal`.
- fact is "Performed Event" on 2024-06-30.                                            // absolute date
- result is "Some Metric" is true.


// Case 3 — multi-anchor (named anchors) for inpatient-style flows.
case "Multi-anchor inpatient-flow scenario":
- description is `Demonstrates named anchors for scenarios with more than
  one meaningful clinical reference point — e.g. admission and discharge —
  and offsets relative to specific named anchors.`.
- subject is "Subject A".
- encounter is "Admission Encounter".
- anchor "admission" is now.
- anchor "discharge" is now + 7 days.
- fact is "Baseline Reading" at "admission".
- fact is "Performed Event" at "admission" + 2 days.
- fact is "Follow-up Reading" at "discharge".
- fact is "Recommended Activity" at "discharge" + 30 days.
- result is "Some Metric" is true.


// Case 4 — cross-resource references, "not done because" link, and the
// documented-contraindication-via-positive-fact pattern.
case "Cross-resource reference scenario":
- description is `Demonstrates the case-scope cross-resource wiring
  vocabulary: `based on`, `part of`, `during encounter`, `requested by`,
  `performed by`, and `not done because`. Also shows the
  documented-contraindication pattern using a positive `DetectedIssue`
  fact rather than a `documented intent` modifier.`.
- subject is "Subject A".
- encounter is "Outpatient Visit".
- anchor is now.
- fact is "Subject A".
- fact is "Contraindication Notation" at anchor - 1 year.
- fact is "Recommended Activity" at anchor with absent intent because `documented contraindication`.
- fact is "Performed Event" at anchor + 3 days.
- "Recommended Activity" based on "Baseline Reading".
- "Performed Event" part of "Recommended Activity".
- "Performed Event" during encounter "Outpatient Visit".
- "Recommended Activity" requested by "Subject A".
- "Performed Event" performed by "Subject A".
- "Recommended Activity" not done because "Contraindication Notation".
- result is "Some Decision" is "Recommended Activity".
- result is "Some Metric" is false.
